#Дизайн_Atom_Inspector_Form<[
Базис:
  LLM и оператор не должны создавать или менять атомы через raw .bvc как основной путь.
  StepAtomDraft JSON уже является безопасным контрактом для formatter-а, validator-а и будущей формы.
  Текущий detail drawer в backlog UI показывает WorkItem как read-only BVC/checks/evidence drilldown, но не является editor-ом.
Вектор:
  Atom inspector form открывает один StepAtomDraft и даёт inspect/edit surface для профилей work_item, charter_section, prompt_rule и trace.
  Форма редактирует profile, name, Базис, Вектор, Цель, labels, checks и evidence как структурированные поля, а не как свободный .bvc text area.
  Для work_item форма дополнительно поднимает основные labels в typed controls: work.id, work.title, work.status, work.owner_role, work.department, work.priority, work.risk, work.depends_on, work.next_action, work.target_files and work.blocker.
  Для charter_section форма поднимает project.* labels: project.slug, project.area, project.phase, project.owner and project.decision where present.
  Для prompt_rule форма поднимает rule.id, protocol.id, design.id and policy-related labels without requiring a new schema profile.
  Для trace форма поднимает trace.status, trace.ref, trace.source, trace.target, trace.kind, trace.evidence and artifact/file refs.
Цель:
  Оператор и LLM могут безопасно править BVC, machine labels, checks and evidence через StepAtomDraft, preview and validation before Work Graph file updates are proposed.

Проверки:
  form covers work_item, charter_section, prompt_rule and trace
  form fields include profile, name, Базис, Вектор, Цель, labels, checks and evidence
  preview includes JSON draft, generated .bvc and validation errors
  save flow proposes Work Graph file update after validator and formatter

Метки:
  atom.profile: plan
  design.id: atom-inspector-form
  design.input: step-atom-draft.v1
  design.input: workgraph.snapshot.v1
  design.related_ui: task-detail-drawer
  work.source: design-atom-inspector-form
  trace.status: verified
]>

#Form_Model_And_Profiles<[
Базис:
  StepAtomDraft v1 keeps the edit model small: profile, name, basis, vector, goal, labels, checks and evidence.
Вектор:
  Header fields: profile select, atom name input, source file, existing atom id/work id if available, dirty state and validation state.
  Semantic core fields: Базис, Вектор and Цель are ordered repeatable single-line rows matching formatter constraints; UI may render multiline visual controls but stores each bullet as one string.
  Checks field: repeatable criteria list mapped to checks and previewed as Проверки.
  Evidence field: repeatable evidence list mapped to evidence and previewed as Свидетельства; structured Evidence v1 records can later provide pickers, but MVP stores strings.
  Labels editor: typed known labels plus advanced key/value rows. Unknown valid labels are preserved and sorted by formatter; invalid keys stay visible with validation errors.
  work_item profile shows task fields first because they drive Work Graph runtime and dashboard cards.
  charter_section profile keeps BVC and project.* labels first because it records project decisions and sections rather than queue state.
  prompt_rule profile highlights rule/protocol/design labels and text intent because these atoms constrain future agents and writers.
  trace profile highlights trace.* labels, evidence/check links and artifact/file refs because trace atoms explain relationships and verification state.
Цель:
  One inspector can edit the shared StepAtomDraft shape while each profile gets a focused field order and shortcuts.

Метки:
  atom.profile: trace
  contract.id: atom-inspector-form-model
  trace.status: verified
]>

#Typed_Label_Shortcuts<[
Базис:
  Метки are the machine envelope for new .bvc writes; shortcuts must make common labels safe without hiding raw labels.
Вектор:
  work.* shortcuts: work.id, work.title, work.status, work.owner_role, work.department, work.priority, work.risk, work.depends_on, work.next_action, work.target_files, work.blocker and work.source.
  trace.* shortcuts: trace.status, trace.ref, trace.source, trace.target, trace.kind, trace.evidence, trace.verified_by and trace.reason.
  project.* shortcuts: project.slug, project.area, project.phase, project.owner, project.decision, project.scope and project.source.
  onebase.* shortcuts: onebase.artifact_kind, onebase.project, onebase.document, onebase.register, onebase.report, onebase.widget, onebase.script, onebase.procedure and onebase.verification_command.
  Shortcuts are typed UI affordances only: they create or edit labels with schema-valid string values and do not add new top-level StepAtomDraft fields.
  Multi-value label shortcuts such as work.depends_on, work.target_files and onebase-related links are edited as chips/lists but serialized as the current comma-separated or project-local string convention until a future schema version changes it.
  Advanced labels remain available for valid keys matching the schema pattern, with warnings for deprecated legacy fields when parser/import work exists.
Цель:
  Operators can edit the labels that matter to Work Graph, trace, project memory and OneBase without memorizing label names or raw .bvc syntax.

Метки:
  atom.profile: prompt_rule
  rule.id: atom-inspector-typed-label-shortcuts
  trace.status: verified
]>

#Preview_And_Validation<[
Базис:
  The inspector must show what will be saved before any file mutation is proposed.
Вектор:
  Preview mode JSON draft shows the exact StepAtomDraft object after form normalization, including inferred or explicit atom.profile label.
  Preview mode generated .bvc runs validateStepAtomDraft then formatStepAtomDraft and displays the canonical block with Базис, Вектор, Цель, optional Проверки/Свидетельства and sorted Метки.
  Preview mode validation errors shows actionable validator messages by field path and blocks save while errors exist.
  The preview should distinguish schema/formatter errors from future Work Graph policy errors such as done without evidence or blocked without blocker reason.
  Warnings are non-blocking and include unknown-but-valid labels, legacy import fields, duplicate semantic values and labels that do not affect the selected profile.
Цель:
  The operator sees JSON, generated .bvc and errors side by side before asking runtime to prepare a file update proposal.

Метки:
  atom.profile: trace
  contract.id: atom-inspector-preview-validation
  trace.status: verified
]>

#Save_Flow<[
Базис:
  The UI must not silently mutate work/backlog.bvc or any other canonical .bvc file.
Вектор:
  Save starts from form state and produces a normalized StepAtomDraft.
  The draft is passed to validateStepAtomDraft; validation errors are returned to the form and no file proposal is created.
  Valid draft is passed to formatStepAtomDraft; the generated block becomes the proposed replacement or insertion payload.
  Runtime/server locates the target atom by source file plus stable imported identity where available: work.id for work_item, design/rule/protocol/contract labels for design atoms, trace.ref/id for trace atoms, or atom name as a last resort after parser support exists.
  The result is a Work Graph file update proposal: target file, old block summary/hash, new generated .bvc block, diff preview, policy warnings and required evidence note.
  Applying the proposal is an explicit operator action and records evidence or an action-feed event; client-side preview never writes canonical state by itself.
  MVP may stop at producing the proposal and diff; later runtime can apply it through a policy-gated endpoint.
Цель:
  Every edit follows draft -> validator -> formatter -> proposed file update, with an auditable approval point before canonical state changes.

Метки:
  atom.profile: prompt_rule
  rule.id: atom-inspector-save-flow
  trace.status: verified
]>

#MVP_Vs_Later<[
Базис:
  The current task is design-only; implementation should stay small and follow existing server/detail drawer boundaries.
Вектор:
  MVP: design the inspector contract, profile field groups, typed label shortcuts, previews, validation states and non-silent save proposal flow.
  MVP implementation later can reuse the existing detail drawer as a read-only entry point and add an "Edit draft" affordance only after parser/import can produce StepAtomDraft from existing .bvc.
  MVP does not require a full browser form now, React dependency, server-side apply endpoint, structured Evidence v1 picker or direct mutation of work/backlog.bvc.
  Later: parser-based import of existing atoms, conflict detection with block hashes, Work Graph policy validation, structured Evidence v1 selector, memory/trace link pickers, OneBase artifact pickers and batch proposal review.
  Later: apply proposal endpoint may update files only after explicit confirmation and runtime policy checks; it must still record evidence/action feed and preserve .bvc as source of truth.
Цель:
  The design unblocks parser/roundtrip and future form implementation without expanding the current read-only drawer into an unsafe editor.

Метки:
  atom.profile: architecture_decision
  decision.id: atom-inspector-mvp-later
  trace.status: verified
]>

#Relation_To_Readonly_Detail_Drawer<[
Базис:
  The backlog UI already has a task detail drawer with Базис, Вектор, Цель, dependencies, checks, evidence, next action, blocker and target files.
Вектор:
  The drawer remains the default read-only inspection surface for WorkItem snapshot data.
  Atom inspector form is a separate edit/review mode opened from the drawer, not a replacement for fast task details.
  The drawer reads derived workgraph.snapshot.v1 fields; the inspector works with StepAtomDraft and generated .bvc previews.
  Until parser roundtrip exists, the drawer can show task details and link to the design artifact, but should not pretend it can safely edit existing atoms.
Цель:
  Read-only task details stay lightweight while structured editing gets a dedicated draft/validation/proposal workflow.

Метки:
  atom.profile: trace
  design.id: atom-inspector-detail-drawer-relation
  trace.status: verified
]>
#Дизайн_Atom_Inspector_Form<[
Базис:
  Человек и LLM не должны hand-write raw .bvc для обычных изменений атомов.
  StepAtomDraft JSON уже является безопасным контрактом ввода для formatter-а и подходит для формы.
  Текущий task detail drawer в backlog UI read-only: он показывает WorkItem BVC/checks/evidence/target files, но не имеет controlled edit flow.
Вектор:
  Atom Inspector Form инспектирует и редактирует StepAtomDraft fields для профилей work_item, charter_section, prompt_rule и trace.
  Форма редактирует только structured draft: profile, name, Базис/basis, Вектор/vector, Цель/goal, labels, checks and evidence.
  Preview показывает три режима: StepAtomDraft JSON, generated .bvc from formatter and validation errors from schema/runtime validator.
  Save flow produces an explicit Work Graph file update proposal after draft -> validator -> formatter; UI never silently mutates .bvc as hidden browser state.
Цель:
  Оператор может безопасно поправить смысл, labels, checks and evidence атома without learning raw .bvc syntax, while canonical storage remains formatter-produced .bvc.

Проверки:
  form purpose covers work_item, charter_section, prompt_rule and trace profiles
  fields include profile, name, Базис, Вектор, Цель, labels, checks and evidence
  preview modes include JSON draft, generated .bvc and validation errors
  save flow is proposal-based and uses validator plus formatter before Work Graph mutation
  read-only detail drawer relation is explicit

Метки:
  atom.profile: plan
  design.id: atom-inspector-form
  design.input: step-atom-draft.v1
  design.output: workgraph-file-update-proposal
  work.source: design-atom-inspector-form
  trace.status: verified
]>

#Supported_Profiles_And_Fields<[
Базис:
  MVP should cover the atom types most likely to be created or edited by an operator and by an LLM-assisted workflow.
Вектор:
  work_item form preset: name, basis, vector, goal, labels.work.id/title/status/owner_role/department/priority/risk/depends_on/target_files/next_action/blocker, labels.trace.status, checks and evidence.
  charter_section form preset: name, basis, vector, goal, labels.project.id/project.area/project.decision/project.risk/trace.status, checks and evidence.
  prompt_rule form preset: name, basis, vector, goal, labels.rule.id/protocol.id/design.id/trace.status, checks and evidence.
  trace form preset: name, basis, vector, goal, labels.trace.status/trace.source.file/trace.source.symbol/trace.confidence/trace.kind, checks and evidence.
  All presets share the same underlying StepAtomDraft fields; profile presets only change labels, helper text, validation hints and shortcut buttons.
  Базис, Вектор and Цель are ordered multiline list editors where each non-empty line becomes one single-line draft string.
  checks and evidence are optional list editors and keep deterministic ordering chosen by the operator until the formatter writes canonical .bvc.
Цель:
  Keep one form model over StepAtomDraft while making common profile fields discoverable and less error-prone.

Метки:
  atom.profile: trace
  contract.id: atom-inspector-supported-profiles-fields
  trace.status: verified
]>

#Typed_Label_Shortcuts<[
Базис:
  Labels are the machine envelope for new writes; legacy top-level machine fields are read/import only.
Вектор:
  work.* shortcuts cover work.id, work.title, work.status, work.owner_role, work.department, work.priority, work.risk, work.depends_on, work.target_files, work.next_action and work.blocker.
  trace.* shortcuts cover trace.status, trace.kind, trace.source.file, trace.source.symbol, trace.confidence, trace.evidence_id and trace.ref.
  project.* shortcuts cover project.id, project.area, project.module, project.decision, project.risk, project.owner and project.version.
  onebase.* shortcuts cover onebase.kind, onebase.name, onebase.document, onebase.register, onebase.report, onebase.widget, onebase.posting_script, onebase.procedure and onebase.verification.
  Generic label editor remains available for valid keys matching the StepAtomDraft label key pattern; unknown keys are allowed but visually separated from typed shortcuts.
  Shortcut chips insert or focus a label row, validate single-line string values and show where labels affect Work Graph runtime, trace, project memory or OneBase adapter projections.
Цель:
  Operators can use typed machine labels without memorizing exact key names, while preserving the flexible labels object required by StepAtomDraft.

Метки:
  atom.profile: prompt_rule
  rule.id: atom-inspector-typed-label-shortcuts
  trace.status: verified
]>

#Preview_And_Validation_Model<[
Базис:
  Safe editing requires immediate feedback before any file proposal is made.
Вектор:
  JSON draft preview shows the exact StepAtomDraft payload the form will submit, including profile, name, basis, vector, goal, labels, checks and evidence.
  Generated .bvc preview calls the same deterministic formatter used by LLM Step Atom Writer; it is disabled or stale-marked when validation fails.
  Validation errors preview combines JSON schema errors, formatter validateStepAtomDraft errors and optional profile-specific warnings.
  Errors are actionable and field-linked: examples include invalid profile, invalid atom name, empty BVC list item, multiline label value, invalid label key and missing work.id for work_item proposal.
  Warnings can show import/read concerns such as legacy fields, unknown label shortcuts, low-confidence trace refs or missing trace.status, but warnings do not silently rewrite the draft.
Цель:
  The operator sees the structured input, canonical output and blockers before asking runtime to update any .bvc file.

Метки:
  atom.profile: trace
  contract.id: atom-inspector-preview-validation
  trace.status: verified
]>

#Save_Flow_And_Update_Proposal<[
Базис:
  Browser UI must not become a hidden source of truth for Work Graph state.
Вектор:
  Save starts from the current form draft and runs draft -> validator -> formatter.
  If validation fails, the form stays editable and only reports validation errors; no file update proposal is created.
  If validation passes, runtime creates a Work Graph file update proposal containing target file path, atom identity, before text when editing an existing atom, generated after text, diff summary, validation evidence and operator action required.
  Applying the proposal is an explicit user/runtime action; it can update work/backlog.bvc or another canonical .bvc file only through the Work Graph writer path.
  Proposal application should record evidence or journal text such as "atom inspector proposal applied" with affected atom id, profile, target file and validation/formatter version.
  Conflict handling compares the current file atom with proposal before text; if the atom changed, runtime asks for rebase/repreview instead of overwriting.
Цель:
  Edits remain auditable and reviewable: the form proposes formatter-produced canonical .bvc, while runtime owns actual file mutation policy.

Метки:
  atom.profile: architecture_decision
  decision.id: atom-inspector-save-proposal-flow
  trace.status: verified
]>

#MVP_Vs_Later_Atom_Inspector<[
Базис:
  This task designs the form, not a broad UI implementation.
Вектор:
  MVP includes profile selector, shared StepAtomDraft fields, typed label shortcuts for work.*, trace.*, project.* and onebase.*, preview tabs, validation errors and proposal-based save contract.
  MVP may attach to the existing read-only detail drawer as an "Edit as draft" affordance only after parser/import support exists; until then the drawer remains read-only and can link to this design.
  MVP does not require React, a new frontend framework, browser-side .bvc parser or direct file writes from the client.
  Later adds .bvc -> StepAtomDraft import/roundtrip, conflict-aware edit sessions, structured Evidence v1 picker, dependency picker, OneBase artifact autocomplete, memory links, bulk edits and schema-driven form generation.
  Later may add a dedicated /api/atom-drafts and /api/atom-proposals pair, but the canonical data path still uses validator, formatter and Work Graph proposal application.
Цель:
  Ship a small safe authoring surface first, then enrich it when parser, evidence and domain adapter producers are available.

Метки:
  atom.profile: architecture_decision
  decision.id: atom-inspector-mvp-later
  next_work: design-step-parser-roundtrip
  trace.status: verified
]>

#Relation_To_Readonly_Detail_Drawer<[
Базис:
  Existing backlog UI already has a task detail drawer that users understand as an inspection surface.
Вектор:
  The current drawer remains read-only in MVP and continues to show task BVC, dependencies, checks, evidence, next action, blocker and target files from workgraph.snapshot.v1.
  Atom Inspector Form is the future edit mode opened from that drawer or from operator dashboard; it should reuse drawer context but use a separate draft/proposal state.
  The drawer can show an "Edit safely" entry point only when the selected atom can be parsed or reconstructed into StepAtomDraft without losing labels, checks or evidence.
  If parser roundtrip is unavailable, the drawer may offer "create new atom from draft" for LLM-generated StepAtomDraft, but should not pretend existing raw .bvc can be edited losslessly.
Цель:
  Preserve the reliable read-only drawer while defining a clear path to structured editing.

Метки:
  atom.profile: trace
  contract.id: atom-inspector-readonly-drawer-relation
  trace.status: verified
]>
